<title>MACAU: A founding member of Macau's casino dies at 93.</title>
<headline>A founding member of Macau's casino dies at 93.</headline>
<dateline>MACAU 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>One of the four founding members of Macau's famed casino, Yip Hon, died of a heart attack in Hong Kong on Wednesday aged 93, Macau casino officials said.</p>
<p>Yip founded the Portuguese-administered enclave's casino monopoly company, Sociedade de Turismo s Diversoes de Macau, together with Stanley Ho, Teddy Yip and Henry Fok in 1961.</p>
<p>STDM has a monopoly of gambling business in Macau until 2001.</p>
</text>
